@startuml
title sd — Trusted ingress address and independent quotas (accepted 2026-10-13)
actor Visitor
participant "Controlled TLS edge" as Edge
participant "Nginx real-IP boundary" as Nginx
participant "Express + existing limiter" as API
Visitor -> Edge: HTTPS request\nPII: transport client IP\nSensitive: cookie / login payload
Edge -> Edge: Overwrite forwarded identity with\ntransport IP and controlled scheme / host
Edge -> Nginx: Forward request from exact configured peer\nPII: canonical client IP
Nginx -> Nginx: Apply real-IP module\nretain original peer address
alt Untrusted peer or no usable replacement
  Nginx --> Edge: 403; do not reach API
  Edge --> Visitor: Generic rejection
else Trusted peer and normalized address
  Nginx -> API: One X-Forwarded-For address\nPII: normalized client IP\nSensitive: existing cookie / payload
  API -> API: Existing session middleware
  API -> API: Trust Nginx socket; select client IP\napply existing per-IP quota
  alt Quota exhausted
    API --> Nginx: 429 + Retry-After
  else Quota available
    API -> API: Existing CSRF / authentication flow
    API --> Nginx: Existing response contract
  end
  Nginx --> Edge: Response
  Edge --> Visitor: HTTPS response
end
note over Visitor, API
  Two different network client IPs -> separate quotas.
  Genuine shared NAT IPs still share a quota.
  Internal transport approval remains a deployment concern.
end note
@enduml
